{
	title: 'Expire edit hints and reconcile informed sessions quietly',
	spec: `Neighbor edit notices are short-lived activity hints, not file ownership. Restored invariant: a reader told that a neighbor modified files hears once when that declaration ends, however long it was idle; a reader that missed the activity hears nothing stale.

A modifies declaration is active for the lifetime of its tool call (bash, EDIT, WRITE, background jobs alike) and for one minute after it ends. A server writing its declared server.log stays declared until its job exits. Turn ends (answer, question, pause, error) neither free nor extend declarations.

Before each model request, a reader in the same cwd hears declared files whose Unix mtime is less than one minute old, whoever changed them: [08-mom (Study cache) modified src/a.ts, src/b.ts <1min ago]. Declared files not modified within the minute are assumed unmodified and not told. Each file is told once while declared; newly modified declared files use the same wording. When told files are no longer declared, the reader hears the shorter of "is no longer editing X" and "is still editing only Y"; when nothing told remains, "is no longer editing files". Lines list at most 5 paths, then N more. Only mtime is checked: no hashes or file kinds.

Notices go through the existing host-notice path and never start or resume a turn. Unchanged state produces no line. State is proportional to live declarations and outstanding reader corrections and is cleared when reconciled. Project-path filtering stays: absolute paths, ~ and Git internals are never told.`,
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'src/host/neighbors.ts: state.active holds one declaration per running tool call (fileChanges.begin starts it; the observation release ends it, so unlaunched and background calls end too); state.told maps reader -> neighbor -> paths last told. notes() diffs told against active and words the change: may be editing / may also be editing / is no longer editing X or is now editing only Y (shorter) / is no longer editing files. turns.ts no longer frees paths at turn end.',
		'Bug 2026-10-08: a 20:51 declared-edits notice made a tab call an idle neighbor editing right now at 21:18, over its own clean git status: the 5-minute expiry was silent and a turn ending in a question freed nothing. bun test src/host/neighbors.test.ts alone fails on an unrelated slash.ts/auth import cycle; it passes in ./test.',
		'mtime check (2026-10-08): neighbors.recent stats declared paths and scans declared globs with Bun.Glob scanSync on each reader request, so notes() stays synchronous and history.ts needs no change. The test sets real mtimes with utimesSync in a temp dir.'
